{
  "dom_id": "step-q214229",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $Z.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9)\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $R$ is reflexive\n\nII. $R$ is symmetric\n\nIII. $R$ is transitive\n\nIV. $R$ is an equivalence relation",
  "worked_solution": "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $x\\in Z,$ $x≡x\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9).$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $x,y\\in Z,$ if $x≡y\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9),$ then $y≡x\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9).$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $x,y,z\\in Z,$ if $x≡y\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9)$ and $y≡z\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9),$ then $x≡z\\,\\,(\\text{mod }9).$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
